r)\" x=\"444\" y=\"412\" width=\"420\" height=\"125\">\n          <text id=\"4:71\" name=\"Activities (04, in this order)\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"4:72\" name=\"Running · 8.00 AM - 9.30 AM · 1.32 hours · 9.50 kilometers Swimming · 8.00 AM - 9.30 AM · 1.32 hours · 9.50 kilometers Cycling · 8.00 AM - 9.30 AM · 1.32 hours · 9.50 kilometers\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"57\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"4:73\" name=\"What is fixed · what is yours\" x=\"64\" y=\"2406\" width=\"1312\" height=\"292\">\n      <text id=\"4:74\" name=\"What is fixed · what is yours\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"328\" height=\"35\" />\n      <frame id=\"4:75\" name=\"Fixed vs yours\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"241\">\n        <frame id=\"4:76\" name=\"Fixed (given)\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"221\">\n          <text id=\"4:77\" name=\"Fixed (given)\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />\n          <text id=\"4:78\" name=\"• Frame list and exact names • Must-include content per frame (what, not how) • Navigation structure and links • All data and copy • Brand color #24C8FE and Inter • Media: illustrations, avatar, photos, icons • Default Button, default Text Field, platform shell\" x=\"24\" y=\"57\" width=\"596\" height=\"140\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"4:79\" name=\"Yours (designer decides)\" x=\"668\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"241\">\n          <text id=\"4:80\" name=\"Yours (designer decides)\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"197\" height=\"23\" />\n          <text id=\"4:81\" name=\"• Layout, grouping, order and emphasis on every screen • All other colors: neutrals, text, backgrounds / surfaces, category tints, activity colors, chart fill, error / disabled • Type scale, spacing, radii, elevation • All states: current tab, selected day, selected hour, pressed, favorited, disabled • Headers, tab bar, activity card, class card, category cards, tags, exercise rows, day pills, chart, activity cards • How photos and cut-outs are cropped, backed and treated\" x=\"24\" y=\"57\" width=\"596\" height=\"160\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"4:82\" name=\"How it is evaluated\" x=\"64\" y=\"2746\" width=\"1312\" height=\"281\">\n      <text id=\"4:83\" name=\"How it is evaluated\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"222\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"4:84\" name=\"Your file is compared with this brief on coverage, data and flow — not on visual similarity to any original.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n      <text id=\"4:85\" name=\"1. Checklist coverage per frame 2. Data &amp; copy accuracy 3. Flow &amp; prototype completeness 4. Information hierarchy 5. Visual quality &amp; consistency of your own system 6. Component reuse 7. State design (current tab, selected day, selected hour)\" x=\"0\" y=\"89\" width=\"1312\" height=\"154\" />\n      <text id=\"4:86\" name=\"Deliverable: the link to your own Figma file containing the 4 named frames, your components and the prototype.\" x=\"0\" y=\"259\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n    </frame>\n  </frame>\n</canvas>"},{"type":"text","text":"IMPORTANT: After you call this tool, you MUST call get_design_context if trying to implement the design, since this tool only returns metadata. If you do not call get_design_context, the agent will not be able to implement the design."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fe9f7e04-3732-4c02-a3aa-681285101806","uuid":"dfa46c60-eef9-41b4-94e7-45d01b8e461a","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:04:00.149Z","tool_use_result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<canvas id=\"0:1\" name=\"00 · Start Here 设计任务\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\">\n  <frame id=\"4:2\" name=\"Start Here · Brief\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1440\" height=\"3091\">\n    <frame id=\"4:3\" name=\"Header\" x=\"64\" y=\"64\" width=\"1312\" height=\"145\">\n      <text id=\"4:4\" name=\"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"182\" height=\"19\" />\n      <text id=\"4:5\" name=\"Workout Class — fitness classes and activity tracking\" x=\"0\" y=\"31\" width=\"1312\" height=\"52\" />\n      <text id=\"4:6\" name=\"Design a fitness class app: get started, find a workout class, open the Warm up category to see its exercises, and review this week’s activity. Canvas 414 × 896, iPhone, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\" x=\"0\" y=\"95\" width=\"1312\" height=\"50\" />\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"4:7\" name=\"How to work\" x=\"64\" y=\"257\" width=\"1312\" height=\"227\">\n      <text id=\"4:8\" name=\"How to work\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"147\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"4:9\" name=\"1. Build exactly the 4 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in screen order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. 3. The brand color and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii and elevation, and apply them consistently. 4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button, a default Text Field and the platform shell (status bar, home indicator). Design all other states, the headers, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file. 5. Use the illustrations, the avatar, the photos and the icons from 04 · Media. 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"176\" />\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"4:10\" name=\"Frames · goals · must include · links\" x=\"64\" y=\"532\" width=\"1312\" height=\"905\">\n      <text id=\"4:11\" name=\"Frames · goals · must include · links\" x=\